---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How it works — LemmaScript"
  description="You and your agent only touch ordinary TypeScript. The model, the proofs, and the fix-and-retry loop are sealed inside the engine — out comes the same code, guaranteed correct."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="kicker">// how it works</span>
      <h1>From TypeScript to <em>math</em> — and back.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        You and your agent only ever touch ordinary TypeScript. Everything in between — the formal model,
        the proofs, the fix-and-retry loop — is sealed inside the engine. What comes out is the same code,
        guaranteed correct.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- the pipeline: input -> black box -> output -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head center" style="margin-inline:auto">
        <span class="kicker">// the pipeline</span>
        <h2>You write the contract. The rest is automatic.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="flow">
        <!-- INPUT — what you / your agent touch -->
        <div class="flow-col">
          <span class="flow-tag">You &amp; your agent write</span>
          <div class="codeblock flow-card">
            <div class="code-bar"><span class="code-file">charge.ts</span></div>
            <pre class="code-body"><span class="t-cmt">//</span><span class="t-at">@</span> <span class="t-dir-contract">contract</span> <span class="t-prose">Never lets the charge exceed the available balance.</span>
<span class="t-cmt">//</span><span class="t-at">@</span> <span class="t-dir-requires">requires</span> <span class="t-annokw">bal &gt;= 0</span>
<span class="t-cmt">//</span><span class="t-at">@</span> <span class="t-dir-requires">requires</span> <span class="t-annokw">amt &gt;= 0</span>
<span class="t-cmt">//</span><span class="t-at">@</span> <span class="t-dir-ensures">ensures</span>  <span class="t-annokw">amt &lt;= bal ==&gt; <span class="t-result">\result</span> === bal - amt</span>
<span class="t-cmt">//</span><span class="t-at">@</span> <span class="t-dir-ensures">ensures</span>  <span class="t-annokw">amt &gt; bal ==&gt; <span class="t-result">\result</span> === 0</span>
<span class="t-kw">function</span> <span class="t-fn">charge</span>(bal, amt) &#123;
  <span class="t-kw">return</span> amt &gt; bal ? <span class="t-num">0</span> : bal - amt;
&#125;</pre>
          </div>
          <p class="flow-note">Ordinary TypeScript with <code class="t-anno">//@</code> contracts. Nothing new to learn.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>

        <!-- BLACK BOX — the engine, fully automatic -->
        <div class="flow-box">
          <div class="flow-box-top">
            <span class="flow-box-name">LemmaScript engine</span>
            <span class="flow-box-auto">automatic</span>
          </div>
          <ol class="flow-steps">
            <li><span class="flow-step-n">1</span><div><b>Compiles</b> to a formal model — Lean 4 or Dafny, from the same source.</div></li>
            <li><span class="flow-step-n">2</span><div><b>Proves</b> every obligation holds — for <em>every</em> input, not a sample.</div></li>
            <li><span class="flow-step-n">3</span><div><b>Iterates</b> — a counterexample sends the agent back to fix and re-run, until green.</div></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="flow-box-foot">// you never touch any of this</p>
        </div>

        <div class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>

        <!-- OUTPUT — what comes out -->
        <div class="flow-col">
          <span class="flow-tag">What ships</span>
          <div class="codeblock flow-card flow-out-card">
            <div class="code-bar"><span class="code-file">charge.ts</span><span class="badge badge-verified" style="margin-left:auto">Verified</span></div>
            <pre class="code-body"><span class="t-kw">function</span> <span class="t-fn">charge</span>(bal, amt) &#123;
  <span class="t-kw">return</span> amt &gt; bal ? <span class="t-num">0</span> : bal - amt;
&#125;</pre>
          </div>
          <p class="flow-note">Your original TypeScript — guaranteed correct for every input.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

    <!-- why -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="kicker">// why it matters</span>
        <h2>What a proof adds to your test suite.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="why-grid">
        <div class="why"><h3>Every input, not just the ones you run</h3><p>Your tests exercise real behavior on the paths you choose. A proof adds what tests can’t: certainty the contract holds for <em>every</em> possible input — including the ones no one thought to try.</p></div>
        <div class="why"><h3>Built for agents</h3><p>LLMs generate plausible code fast. A counterexample is the ground-truth signal an agent needs to converge on correct code instead of confident-but-wrong code.</p></div>
        <div class="why"><h3>Zero runtime cost</h3><p>Verification happens at build time. The shipped artifact is your original TypeScript — no wrappers, no checks, no overhead.</p></div>
        <div class="why"><h3>Drop-in, incremental</h3><p>Annotate one critical function or a whole module. Greenfield or a fork of an existing project — adopt it exactly as far as you want.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="center" style="margin-top:var(--sp-12)">
        <a href="/annotations" class="btn btn-primary">Explore the annotations →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- backends -->
  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="kicker">// two backends, one source</span>
        <h2>Choose the proof system. Keep the same code.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">The annotated TypeScript is the contract. The backend is an implementation detail you can switch without touching your source.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="backend-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-info"><span class="bdot"></span>Lean 4</span>
          <h3>Lean 4</h3>
          <p>A dependently-typed proof assistant with a vast mathematical library. Ideal for deep functional correctness and reusable, composable theorems.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-info"><span class="bdot"></span>Dafny</span>
          <h3>Dafny</h3>
          <p>An automated verification language with an SMT solver under the hood. Ideal for imperative logic, loop invariants, and fast, push-button verification.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ---------- pipeline flow ---------- */
  .flow { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-4); max-width: 760px; margin-inline: auto; }
  .flow-col { width: 100%; max-width: 540px; }
  .flow-tag { display: block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-caption); text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .flow-card .code-body { font-size: var(--fs-small); line-height: 1.7; }
  .flow-out-card { box-shadow: var(--elev-glow); border-color: var(--accent-dim); }
  .flow-note { font-size: var(--fs-caption); color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: var(--sp-3); }
  .flow-note code { font-size: 0.95em; }
  .flow-arrow { color: var(--accent); font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1; }

  /* the engine is dimmed + dashed — it reads as automatic/background, not a hero card */
  .flow-box { width: 100%; max-width: 760px; background: var(--bg-base); border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong); border-radius: var(--r-xl);
    padding: var(--sp-8); position: relative; }
  .flow-box-top { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--sp-3);
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-4); margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); }
  .flow-box-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-body); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .flow-box-auto { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.6rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--text-muted); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--r-full); padding: 2px 8px; }
  .flow-steps { list-style: none; display: grid; gap: var(--sp-6); }
  .flow-steps li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: var(--sp-4); align-items: center;
    font-size: var(--fs-body); color: var(--text-muted); }
  .flow-steps b { color: var(--text-secondary); font-weight: 600; }
  .flow-steps em { font-style: normal; color: var(--accent-bright); }
  .flow-step-n { width: 28px; height: 28px; flex-shrink: 0; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--bg-surface); color: var(--text-muted);
    border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-small); display: grid; place-items: center; }
  .flow-box-foot { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--fs-caption); color: var(--text-faint); margin-top: var(--sp-6); }

  .backend-grid, .why-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: var(--sp-4); }
  .card h3 { margin: var(--sp-3) 0 var(--sp-2); }
  .card p { font-size: var(--fs-small); }
  .why { padding: var(--sp-6); background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: var(--r-lg); }
  .why h3 { font-size: var(--fs-h3); margin-bottom: var(--sp-2); }
  .why p { font-size: var(--fs-small); }
  .why p em { font-style: normal; color: var(--accent-bright); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .backend-grid, .why-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .flow-box { padding: var(--sp-6); }
  }
</style>
